{"id": "unknown-2026-06-10-005", "date": "2026-06-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Crude oil volatility reprices India's polyester textile chain in 2026", "content": "India’s polyester value chain is facing margin pressure as volatile petrochemical feedstocks are driving up costs faster than downstream yarn and apparel prices can adjust. \nWhile PTA, MEG and PET prices surged in H1 2026, fibre and yarn prices rose more gradually. \nPolicy support and MMF export growth offer relief, but apparel makers continue to face challenges in passing higher costs to buyers.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/crude-oil-volatility-reprices-india-s-polyester-textile-chain-in-2026-310900-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-10-006", "date": "2026-06-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh PMI rises to 62.8 in May; all major sectors see expansion", "content": "Economic activity in Bangladesh accelerated in May, with the purchasing managers’ index rising by 8.2 points to 62.8 month on month, indicating a faster pace of expansion across all major sectors.\nThe manufacturing sector posted its second consecutive month of expansion and registered faster growth, supported by stronger increases in new orders, export orders, input purchases and employment.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-pmi-rises-to-62-8-in-may-all-major-sectors-see-expansion-310897-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-10-007", "date": "2026-06-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.75, "keywords": ["decline", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "100% polyester yarn under pressure as crude and feedstock prices fall", "content": "Polyester yarn prices stayed under pressure as falling crude oil prices reduced feedstock costs across the value chain. \nMEG declined sharply, especially in Southeast Asia, lowering polyester production costs. \nEO remained largely stable, while PTA strengthened on firmer demand. The overall trend continues to support softer downstream polyester pricing.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/100-polyester-yarn-under-pressure-as-crude-and-feedstock-prices-fall-310891-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-10-008", "date": "2026-06-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton drops nearly 3% as crude, grain markets weaken", "content": "ICE cotton futures fell nearly 3 per cent as weaker crude oil prices, bearish grain markets and speculative selling pressured sentiment.\nJuly futures settled at 71.26 cents/lb, the lowest intraday level since March 27.\nStrong Brazilian exports, improving US crop conditions and weak risk appetite added pressure.\nTraders now await the USDA WASDE report for fresh market direction.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-drops-nearly-3-as-crude-grain-markets-weaken-310889-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-10-009", "date": "2026-06-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "China Cambodia AEO pact drives 1.97 bn fabric lane for apparel surge", "content": "The Cambodia-China AEO mutual-recognition pact is expected to streamline customs procedures and improve apparel supply-chain efficiency. \nWith China supplying nearly $1.97 billion of textile inputs to Cambodia in January-April 2026, faster clearance and fewer inspections could support garment exports. \nThe deal affirms the importance of customs trust and trade facilitation in apparel competitiveness.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/china-cambodia-aeo-pact-drives-1-97-bn-fabric-lane-for-apparel-surge-310893-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
